# Shot list — "The Paper Lantern"

Timeline target 20.0 s at 24 fps (480 frames). Times are targets; the editor may shift cuts by up to ~0.5 s for rhythm as long as the total stays 18–22 s (aim 19.5–20.5 s). Transitions: short dissolves (~0.5 s) or fades; no hard flashes.

| # | In–Out (s) | Dur | Content (what the frame must show) | Camera move on the still | Sound |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| T | 0.0–2.5 | 2.5 | Opening title "The Paper Lantern" over dusk sky (from shot 1's still, darkened/blurred, or a plain dusk gradient) | slow fade in/out of the title | water + evening ambience fade in |
| 1 | 2.5–6.0 | 3.5 | Wide: calm river at dusk, orange→indigo sky, village of low houses with a few lit windows on far bank, reeds foreground | slow pan right (~5–8% of frame width) | ambience; music cue begins |
| 2 | 6.0–9.5 | 3.5 | Medium: the child kneeling at the river's edge holding the lit paper lantern; amber glow on face and hands | slow push in (~8–10% scale) | ambience, music |
| 3 | 9.5–12.5 | 3.0 | Close: the child's hands releasing the lantern onto the water; ripples; glow reflected | gentle push/drift toward the lantern | soft water touch, music |
| 4 | 12.5–15.5 | 3.0 | Wide-medium: lantern small, floating mid-river past the village; lit windows reflected in the water | slow pan following the drift | ambience, music opens up |
