## Continuity (must hold across shots) — look settled with `production-designer` (director#3)

- **Lantern:** one design everywhere — cuboid ivory paper lantern with thin dark ribs, on a small floating wooden base, warm amber candle light inside. Same shape, colour and glow in shots 2, 3, 4, 5 (in 5 it is only a point of that same amber).
- **Child:** one design everywhere — about seven, dark bobbed hair, rust-red coat, blue trousers; same age and proportions in shots 2 and 3 (hands/sleeves in 3 match the rust-red coat of shot 2). The child may also appear small in shot 1.
- **Style:** textured storybook gouache throughout, one palette: amber lantern and windows against indigo/rose dusk turning to blue-black night. Light gets darker from shot 1 to shot 5 (dusk → night).
- **Geography:** the river flows the same screen direction in shots 1, 3, 4 (left → right), and the village is on the far bank.
- **No text** in any shot picture (no lettering, signatures or watermarks); the title and end card are set by the editor.

## Who makes what

- `production-designer`: a source still per shot (1280x720 or larger) and a **finished silent shot clip per shot**, 1280x720, 24 fps, at least the listed duration + 0.5 s handle on each side for dissolves, with the camera move applied; optionally a background still for the title and end card (no text, leave the central 80% calm for type). Shot log naming each shot's content and move. Published as releases / committed in its repository for the editor to pick up.
- `editor`: title and end-card typography, dissolves, all sound (ambience, music cue, mix), timeline and the rendered cut `film/paper-lantern.mp4`.
- Sound direction: river lapping close in shots 2–3, wider and softer in 4–5; crickets and a faint evening bird early, crickets only later; music a soft, slow cue (e.g. warm felt-piano or music-box notes over a quiet pad, pentatonic, ~60–70 bpm feel), entering in shot 1, lifting gently in shot 4, resolving on a held note into the end card.
